device-samsung-gtactive3wifi: Samsung Galaxy Tab Active3 Wi-Fi (SM-T570)

Early boot (device-samsung-gtactive3wifi-initramfs, also in the Duranium
initrd):
- gtactive3wifi-usb-prep.service: forces the USB 3.0 DRD clock gates on
  (/dev/mem, no clock driver yet), loads exynos-usi + i2c-exynos5 and routes
  the MAX77705 USB-C data switch to the AP over i2c-0 (address 0x25,
  {0x21 0x06 0x09} then {0x41 0x00}), then loads the USB PHY and dwc3.
  Runs once per boot (/run/gtactive3wifi/usb-prep.done). Off:
  gtactive3wifi.usb_prep=0 on the kernel command line.
- RuntimeWatchdogSec=30s on /dev/watchdog0 (PID 1), no reboot/shutdown
  deadline; U-Boot stops the watchdog uniLoader arms.
- gtactive3wifi-initrd-deadline.service (initrd only): reboots to Download
  mode if the initrd has not switched root after 600 s, not counting the
  time a password prompt is open (PID 1 keeps petting the watchdog while
  the initrd waits forever for a missing root disk). Off:
  gtactive3wifi.initrd_deadline=0.
- 90-gtactive3wifi-nested-gpt.rules: exposes the GPT nested in the
  userdata partition as a partitioned loop device.

Booted system:
- Suspend to idle only (PSCI 0.1: no deeper state, no hibernation), and only
  once the wake-up path has been proven on this tablet:
  gtactive3wifi-suspend-gate.service allows it for a boot when the kernel
  can freeze, the power key is a wake-up source and
  /var/lib/gtactive3wifi/suspend-wake-proven exists (written after the
  on-device suspend test). Power key: suspend, long press: power off; the
  book cover (SW_LID) suspends. After a sleep, gtactive3wifi-usb-resume
  makes sure the USB debug link is enumerated again. dwc3 and the UFS disks
  keep runtime PM off (60-gtactive3wifi-pm.rules).
- regulator_ignore_unused until the first ACPM regulator write is proven.
- Cameras: libcamera simple pipeline + SoftISP (the CSIS driver reports a
  driver name libcamera knows; SoftISP tuning for S5K3L6 and GC5035).
- UI-neutral: one device package for every image variant (UI=gnome,
  UI=phosh, ...). PAN_MESA_DEBUG=noafbc for gdm, greetd and user sessions.
- device-samsung-gtactive3wifi-gnome (installs itself with
  postmarketos-ui-gnome): fast-animations@gtactive3wifi (St slow-down
  factor 0.6), Blur my Shell and Touchup enabled by default, IBus Typing
  Booster (gschema override).
- Home and Recent keys: app grid and overview in GNOME Shell, overview in
  Phosh (org.gnome.shell.keybindings, read by both).
- kernel.panic=10 (Alpine's sysctl.d sets 120 s): a panic reboots quickly
  and boot counting can fall back.
- New users get /bin/bash (/etc/default/useradd).
- gtactive3wifi-switch-ui UI: switch to another UI image (phosh, gnome) with the
  A/B update (sysupdate with the other UI's channel); /etc/os-release is never
  edited (the next boot's base confext is checked against it).
- gtactive3wifi-firmware-import.service: installs the owner's Samsung
  firmware that the installer (setup.sh) left on the ESP
  (gtactive3wifi-firmware.tar.zst + .sha256) into /var/lib/firmware before
  udev loads the drivers when /var/lib/firmware is empty or holds an
  older import (hand-installed firmware is kept); checked, swapped in whole;
  the tarball stays on the ESP, so a fresh root gets it again.
- gtactive3wifi-extensions-link.service: links the sysext/confext images
  of this image version from /var/lib/duranium-extensions into
  /run/extensions and /run/confexts before systemd-sysext/-confext merge
  (scripts/duranium-update delivers them with each A/B update).

Battery and responsiveness (both UIs):
- workqueue.power_efficient=1: power-hungry per-CPU work runs on a CPU
  that is awake instead of waking an idle one.
- No modem: ModemManager and the user daemons for SMS/MMS, visual
  voicemail and cell broadcasts are disabled (presets).
- systemd-oomd prefers apps over GNOME Shell, Phosh and gnome-session
  (ManagedOOMPreference=avoid); zram swap and its sysctls come from
  postmarketos-zram (zstd, 150 % of RAM, swappiness 180).
- Power profiles (tuned-ppd): "power-saver" caps the A55 at 1456 MHz
  (Samsung's energy table: 25-34 % more energy per cycle above it),
  "performance" keeps the zram-friendly memory settings
  (/etc/tuned/profiles, each including the stock TuneD profile).

Containers (device-samsung-gtactive3wifi-containers, recommended by the
device package, so every image has it):
- podman, rootless for every user (subordinate IDs from useradd) and
  rootful for root.
- Alpine (docker.io/library/alpine:3.24 and :latest) preinstalled as an OCI
  layout in /usr/lib/gtactive3wifi/container-images/alpine (Alpine's
  minirootfs as the layer, mkoci.sh), loaded once per image version into
  root's store at boot (gtactive3wifi-container-images.service) and into
  each user's store at login (the user unit of the same name), so
  "podman run --rm alpine cat /etc/alpine-release" works offline.
- /usr/libexec/gtactive3wifi/containers-selftest: offline checks for the
  calling user (run it as root and as the user).
